window.docContents[48].resolve({"/LindenstraussPolynomials/Alpha/#mod-doc-LindenstraussPolynomials___Alpha-1-0":{"contents":"The step sizes\n\nThe perturbations of the construction use the step sizes \\alpha_k=a^{2^k} for a fixed a\\in(0,1), so that \\alpha_{k+1}=\\alpha_k^2; this identity is used essentially in the inductive step. The module proves the tail estimates (eq:tails) and the product estimate (eq:product). Indices start at 0: \\alpha_0=a is the article's \\alpha_1.\n\n\n","context":"","header":"LindenstraussPolynomials.Alpha","id":"/LindenstraussPolynomials/Alpha/#mod-doc-LindenstraussPolynomials___Alpha-1-0"}});